I ascended this rather ridiculous game last Saturday (08.12.06).  After
re-reading my notes and re-watching the (post-castle) .ttyrec's I've
gotten around to inflicting a not-so-brief write up upon rgrn.
Hopefully you are amused.

Without much more ado, on to the good parts!

-cdi, appreciative of any commentary/critiques/questions/&c

P.S. I appologize in advance if the console->gVim->usenet copy/paste
routine inserts a lot of garbage into the source text.

****

Grimley started off with a magic marker (0:91).  Within the first five
dungeon levels, the RNG provided him with a magic lamp, some blank
paper, a bag of holding, and a second magic marker (later ID'd as
(0:98) ... yes, this game was that absurd :-).  But no weapons or
armour, not even the usual goblin death drop of an orcish helm, which
was annoying.

Upon descending to Dlvl.06, Grimley was quickly trapdoored down to
Dlvl.08 ... right by the downstair.  Dropped down, came back up, and
found the sokoban upstair before the main dungeon upstair.  Sokoban was
the reflection variant (I love it when a plan comes together!).  On the
way up, a brown pudding proceeded to rot his armour (AC:10), which
kinda sucked.

While leaving sokoban, a hostile 'h' (generated that way?) dropped a
complete set of dwarvish armour (cloak, shield, helm, shoes, and
mithril) and a dwarvish short sword.  That made up for the pathetic
start (kit wise).

