Now is when the real fun starts ...

The level just below minetown was a double bones level.  The first
bones pile (Agavi, killed by a soldier ant) had a cursed long sword and
a cursed magic lamp.  The second bones pile (Grimley (no relation),
killed by a soldier ant) contained Dragonbane and a *TWO* cursed magic
lamps.  The same cheeky soldier ant took out both PC's.

// Aside, the Grimley bones pile was from my one and only attempt at
// the Minetown Protection Run.  I made it without leveling up, went
// down a level, and promptly got stomped.

Instead of doing mines end, it was time for a side-trip back up to
Dlvl.01 to convert an altar, blank some potions (pick-axed fountain),
and alchemize some b!full healing, and (uncursed) genocide 'h' and 'h'.
 ("I'm sorry, I know we're distantly related.  But brain-sucking
humanoids are evil, and must be punished.")

After Dlvl.01 altar was converted a test #offer to confirm prayer
safety left him with the blessed rustproof +0 Demonbane.  That, ladies
and gentlemen, unrestricted longsword.  Huzzah! Huzzah!

After getting some holy water for the 5 non-blessed magic lamps, wishes
#2 and #3 were spent on a spellbook of identify and a rustproof helm of
brilliance.

Between the two magic markers and several scrolls of enchant armour and
enchant weapon Grimley had chanced across already, it was a trivial
exercise to get Demonbane to +7 and the Helm of Brilliance to +5 (both
safely, to boot!).  The first three attempts at getting a ring of
increase damage to +7 or higher failed miserably.

Did I mention finding eleven scrolls of charging?  No? Perhaps I should
have.

Along the way to mines end, a barrow wight kindly dropped a 2nd long
sword (+3 to boot!).  The aforementioned long sword promptly became +7,
rustproof, and Grimley's alternate weapon.  (The 1st was still cursed).

After clearing out mines end (Mimic of the Mines, for those who care),
it was time to start #dipping for Excalibur.  Apparantly, the lady of
the lake was busy, because she sent a proxy:

